<handout xml:id="pp-specs-printable">
<title>Writing Conventions for MTH 210</title>
<page>

 <paragraphs>  
  <title>Required writing conventions</title>
  
	<p>These are writing conventions that we will learn and use in MTH 210. Every writing revision and final revision of each portfolio should follow all of these.</p>
	
	<p>See the full document on Blackboard for detailed explanations and examples.</p>


  
  	<p>To earn <q>math &amp; writing successful</q> or better, a proof must do <em>all</em> of these:</p>
	
	<p><xref ref="wc-statement" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	<p><xref ref="wc-assumptions" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	<p><xref ref="wc-proof-method" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	<p><xref ref="wc-justify" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	<p><xref ref="wc-variables" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	<p><xref ref="wc-definitions" text="type-local-title" /></p>

</paragraphs>
</page>
	

<page>
<paragraphs>
	<title>Additional writing conventions</title>
	
		<p>Every proof must do <em>most</em> of these, where <q>most</q> means occasional errors in up to 3 items, or consistent errors in 1 item.</p>
		<p>One way to earn <q>excellent</q> is for a proof to do <em>all</em> of these thoroughly and with no noticeable omissions.</p>
	
	<p><xref ref="wc-overleaf" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	<p><xref ref="wc-spelling" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	<p><xref ref="wc-we" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	<p><xref ref="wc-begin" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	<p><xref ref="wc-formula" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	<p><xref ref="wc-display" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	<p><xref ref="wc-symbols" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	<p><xref ref="wc-numbering" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	<p><xref ref="wc-textbook-format" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	<p><xref ref="wc-italics" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	<p><xref ref="wc-summary" text="type-local-title" /></p>
	
</paragraphs>
</page>	

</handout>
